  "provenance": {
    "pattern": "dubstep: the half-time grid of a 140 track — kick on one, snare on the third beat — under a wobbling sub, here re-struck in eighths and sixteenths where the genre sweeps a filter with an LFO",
    "knowledge": "public knowledge of the genre: the pattern as drummers, producers and tutorials commonly write it; no recording was sampled, transcribed from audio or mined",
    "note": "Two bars: kick one and a late kick before the second bar, snare on beat three of each bar, eighth hats with a sixteenth pickup. The wobble is the genre's filter moved by an LFO in eighths or triplets; the kitchen has no LFO on a bass voice, so the row approximates it by re-striking the sub: eighths through the first bar, sixteenths into a held note in the second. It plays at 130 under the Dub key: 140 is out of every band."
  }
